    fix(CF-183): certify the pinned harness, not any hermes on PATH
    
    The PATH fallback was silently treated as adapter-owned, the version row
    accepted any banner without comparing HERMES_PIN, and --apply used binary
    presence rather than venv ownership and the measured pin to skip install.
    Distinguish host-provided binaries, compare the measured version token with
    the pin, and install when the venv binary is missing or mismatched. Preserve
    build-metadata banners and the existing absent/installed fixture rows.
    
    Selftest section 31b is RED against the original script and GREEN with this
    fix. It covers host and venv ownership, matching and mismatched versions,
    real Hermes banner metadata, exact pinned pip arguments, fresh-HOME venv
    creation despite PATH hermes, and retention only of a matching owned pin.
    Correct README's host-binary claim and the harness spec in the same change.
    
    Full selftest and board validation pass. Ruff lint passes; format check
    flags the unchanged cf181-verdict-binding-sweep.py at the original tip too.
    The real Python 3.12 probe creates a venv and installs 0.19.0; its subsequent
    check passes binary/version and still fails the absent port/provider key.
    
    A commit cannot embed its own SHA: commit=none:self-referential-hash is
    explicit because this delivery requires one commit and forbids amending.
    The actual commit SHA is reported separately.
    
